& [Situation]
  + resident-service RS-009 and self-hosted corpus workflows are independently complete but the published product acceptance lacks one release-bound disposable end-to-end command

& [Justification]
  + the smallest private-beta gain is orchestration evidence over existing semantics rather than a new feature or service

& [Solution]
  + build or admit four exact local binaries stage them into one closed disposable root compile the tracked corpus run authenticated service health and query stop prove direct fallback then safely remove the root

& [Delineation]
  + fixture signing seeds prove mechanics not production trust custody
  + local loopback service execution is inside; provider network remote effects persistence FPGA and Minecraft are outside
  + filesystem rollback is exact removal of the workflow-owned disposable root after graceful stop not an upgrade or production recovery claim

& [Decision]
  + activate additive workflow verifier tests checked evidence runbook and proof only
